        "translations": {
          "en": {
            "seby": {
              "text": "The little prince sweeps his volcanoes clean. Then he flies away with a flock of wild birds."
            },
            "ale": {
              "text": "Before leaving, the little prince carefully sweeps out his three volcanoes. As he says goodbye, the rose confesses her love at last and declines the glass globe to welcome butterflies."
            },
            "emma": {
              "text": "For his escape he took advantage of a migration of wild birds. On the morning of his departure he carefully swept out his two active volcanoes and his extinct volcano. \"Goodbye,\" he said to the flower. \"Of course I love you,\" she replied. \"Try to be happy... Leave that globe alone.\""
            }
          }
        },
        "questions": null
