        "translations": {
          "en": {
            "seby": {
              "text": "The vain man lifts his hat for applause. The drunkard sits sadly beside empty bottles."
            },
            "ale": {
              "text": "On the second planet, the vain man hears nothing but praise and tips his hat. On the third planet, a silent drunkard drinks endlessly just to forget how ashamed he feels."
            },
            "emma": {
              "text": "Conceited people never hear anything but praise. The next planet was inhabited by a tippler, settled in silence before empty bottles and full bottles. \"Why are you drinking?\" \"To forget that I am ashamed,\" the tippler confessed. \"Ashamed of what?\" \"Ashamed of drinking!\" Grown-ups are certainly very, very odd."
            }
          }
        },
        "questions": null
