        "translations": {
          "en": {
            "seby": {
              "text": "At dawn they discover a singing well. Its cool water tastes sweet like a lovely gift."
            },
            "ale": {
              "text": "At daybreak they discover a real village well in the sand. As the pilot hauls up the heavy bucket, the old pulley sings softly, and the cool water feels like a festive gift."
            },
            "emma": {
              "text": "\"Do you hear,\" said the little prince, \"we have wakened this well, and it is singing...\" This water was born of the walk beneath the stars, the song of the pulley, and the effort of my arms. It was good for the heart. \"Eyes are blind; look with the heart.\""
            }
          }
        },
